Report read errors in shuf.
A read error ends the line reader's input just as end of file does, and
shuf never checked the stream's error flag, so it shuffled whatever had
been read and exited 0. Check the result of fclose_if_not_stdin(),
which reports the error flag, and die with the file name, as shuf
already does when the file cannot be opened.

---
 coreutils/shuf.c |    3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/coreutils/shuf.c
+++ b/coreutils/shuf.c
@@ -197,7 +197,8 @@
 			lines = xrealloc_vector(lines, 6, numlines);
 			lines[numlines++] = line;
 		}
-		fclose_if_not_stdin(fp);
+		if (fclose_if_not_stdin(fp))
+			bb_simple_perror_msg_and_die(fname);
 	}
 
 	outlines = numlines;
